('acbcfc51-7773-5635-982e-f08aa8378879'::uuid,'1e6d98b2-b29d-52c9-9f6d-537cf7b2e265'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.6)',E'# ANNEX 3-M \\| Source and Methodology Register\n\n| **Source**                                                                        | **Verified use in this chapter**                                                                                          | **Status / qualification**                                                                                                                     |\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Republic Act No. 10121 (2010), Lawphil / Supreme Court E-Library                  | Statutory LDRRMC and LDRRMO functions; risk assessment, risk information, local risk map, LDRRMP and contingency planning | Official statutory text; apply with current IRR                                                                                                |\n| DHSUD Memorandum Circular No. 2025-004, Enhanced CDRA Policy                      | Policy intent and minimum approach for standardized enhanced CDRA                                                         | DHSUD learning repository confirms policy purpose; obtain signed circular and annexes for exact operative requirements                         |\n| DHSUD CDRA learning repository: 5-Step+ CDRA Process                              | Detailed sequence for CDRA steps and subsequent compilation, CLUP mainstreaming, M&E and communication                    | Official DHSUD training material; apply current technical parameters and prescribed tools                                                      |\n| PHIVOLCS GIS hazard-map download instructions and Hazard Assessment Services      | Source acquisition, product scale/availability caveats and limits of hazard assessment reports                            | Official PHIVOLCS pages; not a substitute for current technical manuals                                                                        |\n| DILG MC No. 2025-035 / Listo si KAP information                                   | Barangay preparedness and planning responsibilities                                                                       | DILG regional publication confirms initiative; use signed circular and current national quality tools                                          |\n| DILG Quality Assessment System / BDRRM plan template                              | Barangay plan review structure and quality assurance                                                                      | Use current official versions; legacy templates are not presumed current                                                                       |\n| OCD/NDRRMC PSCP Guidebook                                                         | Essential functions, BIA and continuity planning                                                                          | Listed in IAT References as project reference; exact edition and original file must be verified before final technical sign-off                |\n| OCD/NDRRMC contingency-planning manual                                            | Hazard scenario and response planning method                                                                              | Exact edition and original file not located in retrieved project materials; obtain from OCD Region VIII and reconcile this SOP before approval |\n| UNDRR Disaster Resilience Scorecard for Cities – Detailed Level Assessment (2017) | Good-practice benchmarks for scenarios, critical asset failure chains, risk-sensitive planning and ecosystem services     | Benchmark only; IAT crosswalk identifies its adapted indicators                                                                                |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v1_Annex_3-M.md (Chapter 3, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.6))','draft'),
('5e347d74-8336-5a24-9452-e9c89aa769c0'::uuid,'3189595e-e334-59f9-829b-ac4fb4757c40'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.6)',E'# ANNEX 3-N \\| Glossary of Terms Used in This Chapter\n\nTerms follow RA 10121, the DHSUD CDRA guidance and the definitions used in Chapters 1 and 2. Where an official definition exists, it governs.\n\n**Table 3.12**\n\n*Glossary of Terms*\n\n| **Term**                                    | **Meaning in this Manual**                                                                                                                                  |\n|---------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Adaptive capacity                           | The ability of people, institutions and systems to adjust to, prepare for and recover from hazard and climate impacts.                                      |\n| BIA (business impact analysis)              | Assessment of how the disruption of an essential function affects people and the City over time; the basis for recovery priorities (Form 3-07).             |\n| CDRA (Climate and Disaster Risk Assessment) | The DHSUD-prescribed assessment that links hazard and climate information to exposure, vulnerability and risk, and to land-use decisions.                   |\n| Contingency plan                            | An approved, hazard-specific plan setting scenario, triggers, roles, resources and reporting before an event (SOP 3-6).                                     |\n| Critical point facility / lifeline          | A facility (hospital, school, EOC) or network (road, power, water, telecommunications) whose failure affects many people or services.                       |\n| Exposure                                    | People, buildings, production areas, facilities and lifelines located where a hazard may occur.                                                             |\n| Failure chain                               | A traced sequence from a hazard through an asset failure to a service disruption and its consequences (SOP 3-4).                                            |\n| Form                                        | The record a step is closed on. In MODE every workflow and protocol step has a form; the Manual''s form where one exists, otherwise the one-tap step record. |\n| MDA (Major Decision Area)                   | A place or issue where CDRA results require a land-use, investment, social-protection or ecosystem decision (Form 3-04).                                    |\n| Modelled potential damage                   | The value of exposed assets that could be damaged under a model''s assumptions; not an observed loss or an annual expected loss.                             |\n| Process owner                               | The office accountable for an SOP producing its result; others are responsible, consulted or informed (Section 18).                                         |\n| Protocol                                    | A step-by-step operational checklist run at the point of action (for example warning dissemination); it records who closed each step and when.              |\n| PSCP (Public Service Continuity Plan)       | The City plan that keeps essential functions running during disruption (SOP 3-7).                                                                           |\n| Risk Information Register                   | The controlled list of risk datasets with source, custodian, date, scale, access class and version (SOP 3-2).                                               |\n| SOP (standard operating procedure)          | The approved, controlled text in the Manual that states what is done, by whom, under what authority and with what records.                                  |\n| Validation status                           | How far information has been checked: reported, preliminary, field-verified or official (Geo-COP layers; IAT evidence).                                     |\n| Workflow                                    | An SOP made executable in MODE: a sequence of steps across offices over days or weeks, each closed on its form.                                             |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v1_Annex_3-N.md (Chapter 3, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.6))','draft'),
('5db2c406-34ae-5bc1-980f-092e3b0d38ab'::uuid,'b76900a1-d745-5b8a-a3bd-09b1b25792f2'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-A \\| Indicator-to-Process Traceability Matrix\n\n| **IAT ref** | **Requirement**                                           | **Chapter process**                                    | **Process owner / interface**                | **Evidence required**                                                        |\n|-------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| A3.1        | LDRRMP current, approved and aligned                      | LDRRMP review and mainstreaming (SOP 3-5)              | CDRRMO / CDRRMC; CPDO interface              | Approved plan, resolution, alignment crosswalk, annual review                |\n| A3.2        | DRR-CCA mainstreamed in CLUP/CDP/ELA/LCCAP and investment | CDRA Step 7; investment screening (SOP 3-5)            | CPDO/LDC; CDRRMO technical input             | CDRA-to-plan crosswalk, zoning/plan decisions, screening records             |\n| A3.3        | Hazard-specific contingency plans and testing             | Contingency plan development (SOP 3-6)                 | CDRRMO coordinator; hazard leads             | Approved plans, exercise reports, corrective-action register                 |\n| A3.4        | PSCP covers CDRRMO and essential City services            | PSCP (SOP 3-7)                                         | Continuity executive; department heads       | Essential functions inventory, BIA, PSCP, exercise                           |\n| A3.7        | Barangay DRRM plans reviewed/consolidated                 | Barangay QA (SOP 3-8)                                  | BDRRMC/BDC; CDRRMO and DILG review           | Verified master list, official QA tool, status matrix                        |\n| A5.1        | Updated multi-hazard maps at barangay scale               | Hazard mapping (SOP 3-1); repository (SOP 3-2)         | CDRRMO GIS; source agencies                  | Validated map package, metadata and version register                         |\n| A5.2        | CDRA with exposure and vulnerability                      | CDRA (SOP 3-3); impact-chain analysis                  | CPDO/CDRA TWG; CDRRMO                        | CDRA report, geodatabase, risk tables, MDAs                                  |\n| A5.3        | Disaggregated at-risk population database                 | CDRA exposure database; inclusion (SOP 3-9)            | CBMS/data custodian; CSWDO/Health; barangays | Current lawful dataset, data dictionary, privacy review                      |\n| A5.8        | Critical facilities and dependency/failure-chain map      | Critical facilities (SOP 3-4)                          | Asset owners/utilities; CDRRMO coordinates   | Asset register, dependency diagram, failure-chain sheets                     |\n| A7.6        | Inclusive DRRM embedded in plans and services             | Inclusive assessment (SOP 3-9); all plan SOPs          | Sector offices; CDRRMO; representatives      | Accessible consultation records, plan provisions, barrier closure            |\n| C1.1        | Risk scenarios inform CDP/CLUP and investments            | CDRA MDA and planning interface (SOP 3-3/SOP 3-5)      | CPDO/LDC                                     | Scenario register and plan/investment crosswalk                              |\n| C1.2        | DRR/CCA screening in project and budget approval          | Investment screening (SOP 3-5)                         | CPDO; Budget/LFC; technical regulators       | Screening form, LDC/LFC minutes, appraisal record                            |\n| C1.3        | Loss analysis beyond physical assets                      | Exposure/loss analysis (SOP 3-3)                       | CPDO and sector data owners                  | Livelihood, jobs, displacement, agriculture, ecosystem and heritage analysis |\n| C1.4        | Risk-sensitive zoning and permit guidelines               | Hazard map use (SOP 3-1); planning interface (SOP 3-5) | CPDO/Zoning; Engineering/OBO                 | Adopted overlays/guidelines and sample permit review                         |\n| C3.1        | Protective ecosystems identified and monitored            | Inclusive/ecosystem interface (SOP 3-9)                | CENRO/DENR; City Agriculture                 | Ecosystem register, baseline and annual monitoring report                    |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-A.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('97046567-47cb-5ae5-bb78-daa953bb3bdd'::uuid,'e0e7eae4-41d7-57cf-a334-3a71d73c4917'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-B \\| Form 3-01 – Risk Information and Map Request\n\n| **Field**               | **Required entry**                                               | **Field**                        | **Required entry**                                   |\n|-------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------|\n| Request ID / date       | Unique ID and date received                                      | Requesting office / focal person | Name, designation and contact                        |\n| Decision purpose        | Screening / public information / CLUP / technical review / other | Hazard / geography               | Hazard, barangay(s), coordinates or area             |\n| Required scale / format | Scale, map format, GIS format and output                         | Required-by date                 | Date and reason                                      |\n| Source product          | Agency, product title, version/date, URL/reference               | Limitations                      | Scale, uncertainty, no-data, restrictions            |\n| Validation office       | Technical reviewer and review date                               | Approval/use category            | Internal / public / planning / regulatory            |\n| Release details         | Version, date, distribution and custodian                        | Revision trigger                 | Source update / event / boundary change / correction |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-B.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft')
insert into public.moo_versions (id,document_id,label,body_md,change_note,status) values
('74476b25-8fb4-522e-ae8b-56bcafd59fac'::uuid,'9f3a52ba-ab8e-531a-ad9a-84833f0a6ea5'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-C \\| Form 3-02 – Dataset Metadata and Quality Checklist\n\n| **Metadata / quality field**                   | **Check / entry**                                     |\n|------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|\n| Dataset ID, title and description              | Record unique ID, purpose and content                 |\n| Source agency and original product reference   | Record issuing authority and original file            |\n| Data date, acquisition date and update cycle   | Distinguish source date from download date            |\n| Geographic coverage and scale/resolution       | Record City/barangay coverage and suitability         |\n| Coordinate reference system and units          | Record original CRS and any transformation            |\n| Method, scenario, baseline and time horizon    | Record model/method assumptions and projection period |\n| Attributes, legend and classification          | Check classes, units, code lists and interpretation   |\n| Completeness, geometry and no-data areas       | Record defects and treatment                          |\n| Limitations and uncertainty                    | Record known constraints and prohibited uses          |\n| Custodian, access classification and retention | Record responsible office and access controls         |\n| Technical validation and approval              | Reviewer, date, comments and approved use             |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-C.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('33da72b2-f75d-557c-9000-6270604cd483'::uuid,'e7b3e024-7d39-52cf-a4ee-55550a7c16b8'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-D \\| Form 3-03 – CDRA Hazard-Impact Scoping Matrix\n\n| **Hazard / climate stressor** | **Source / scenario / horizon** | **Affected sectors / elements**                          | **Impact chain and spatial area**           | **Data gap / uncertainty**    | **Validation owner** |\n|-------------------------------|---------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------------------|----------------------|\n| \\[Enter hazard\\]              | \\[Source, date, scenario\\]      | \\[People, buildings, livelihoods, services, ecosystems\\] | \\[Initiating event → impact → consequence\\] | \\[Missing data / confidence\\] | \\[Office / agency\\]  |\n| \\[Enter hazard\\]              | \\[Source, date, scenario\\]      | \\[People, buildings, livelihoods, services, ecosystems\\] | \\[Initiating event → impact → consequence\\] | \\[Missing data / confidence\\] | \\[Office / agency\\]  |\n\nInstructions: Complete one row per hazard-sector pathway. Identify assumptions and data gaps explicitly. Do not assign risk classes outside the current DHSUD-prescribed method.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-D.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('7844d7dd-94d9-5b3e-a958-890d3801fdf9'::uuid,'90c1dec6-06ac-5832-a1f9-8b356a61d78e'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-E \\| Form 3-04 – CDRA Major Decision Area Register\n\n| **MDA ID / location**            | **Evidence and risk finding**     | **Affected people/assets / system** | **Policy or investment decision required**                                              | **Lead office / partners** | **Indicator / target / review date** |\n|----------------------------------|-----------------------------------|-------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------|--------------------------------------|\n| \\[ID / barangay / spatial unit\\] | \\[CDRA result and map reference\\] | \\[Disaggregated groups and assets\\] | \\[Land-use, infrastructure, social protection, ecosystem or preparedness intervention\\] | \\[Owner\\]                  | \\[Measure and due date\\]             |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-E.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('097fb08d-b32f-54a9-83c8-903d303d00c0'::uuid,'46a8c9fd-c613-58c1-9879-078061eecd35'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-F \\| Form 3-05 – Critical Facilities and Dependency Register\n\n| **Asset ID / name** | **Owner / operator** | **Service / capacity / users**       | **Hazard exposure / vulnerability** | **Dependencies / downstream services**            | **Backup / redundancy / restoration**        | **Validation date**  |\n|---------------------|----------------------|--------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|----------------------|\n| \\[ID\\]              | \\[Office / utility\\] | \\[Function, capacity, service area\\] | \\[Map/source and condition\\]        | \\[Power, water, telecom, road, fuel, staff, ICT\\] | \\[Alternate, backup, estimated restoration\\] | \\[Date / signatory\\] |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-F.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('6dde3b7c-8e48-574b-9d2d-d99675258a9c'::uuid,'9408a317-5f2d-5396-bfd1-9eaad44254d6'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-G \\| Form 3-06 – Contingency Plan Quality and Exercise Record\n\n| **Control area**                     | **Required evidence / reviewer finding**                                         | **Status / corrective action** |\n|--------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n| Scenario and assumptions             | Source, magnitude, location, lead time, cascading effects and uncertainty        |                                |\n| Objectives and concept of operations | Priorities, phases, EOC/ICS interface and transition                             |                                |\n| Roles and tasking                    | Lead/support agencies, barangay roles, escalation and alternates                 |                                |\n| Triggers and warning                 | Authoritative source, action threshold, decision authority and dissemination     |                                |\n| Operations and protection            | Evacuation, shelter, health, logistics, protection, MHPSS and public information |                                |\n| Resources and logistics              | Personnel, equipment, supplies, transport, facilities and gaps                   |                                |\n| Information management               | Situation reporting, validation, decision log and records                        |                                |\n| Exercise results                     | Objectives, observations, decisions, performance and lessons                     |                                |\n| Corrective actions                   | Action, owner, deadline, resource and closure evidence                           |                                |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-G.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('31c573d9-1aff-5607-9742-a6cee4322fda'::uuid,'84f5dd93-d2d8-5de7-b21a-e2ff7911517c'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-H \\| Form 3-07 – Essential Functions Inventory and BIA\n\n| **Department / service** | **Essential function / legal basis** | **Service users / minimum level**          | **People / skills / succession** | **Facilities / ICT / records** | **Dependencies / suppliers**                 | **Impact over time / priority**                        | **Recovery strategy / owner**  |\n|--------------------------|--------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|----------------------------------|--------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n| \\[Office\\]               | \\[Function and authority\\]           | \\[Who depends on service; minimum output\\] | \\[Key posts, alternates\\]        | \\[Site, system, records\\]      | \\[Power, water, telecom, transport, vendor\\] | \\[Life safety, legal, welfare, financial; time bands\\] | \\[Strategy, owner, resources\\] |\n\nInstructions: Department head validates each function. Proposed recovery time and minimum service levels must be justified by BIA evidence and approved by the designated continuity executive; do not use unsupported generic time targets.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-H.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('3a207140-3a65-57b6-9883-db155bbed9a1'::uuid,'ae91e295-4eee-5511-965a-8a53ea3b2b19'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-I \\| Form 3-08 – Barangay DRRM Plan Review Status\n\n| **Barangay official name / ID** | **Master-list source** | **Plan period / version** | **Approval evidence** | **Quality tool / review date** | **Status** | **Required corrections / due date** | **Exercise / update evidence** |\n|---------------------------------|------------------------|---------------------------|-----------------------|--------------------------------|------------|-------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n| \\[Barangay\\]                    | \\[Official source\\]    | \\[Period/version\\]        | \\[Resolution/date\\]   | \\[Tool/version/date\\]          | \\[Status\\] | \\[Action and due date\\]             | \\[Record\\]                     |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-I.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('01b041b7-4f53-5b38-9d52-90a2cdd9cf68'::uuid,'62fd7931-d11e-5a0f-b471-804bba6800ea'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-J \\| Form 3-09 – DRR/CCA Project Screening\n\n| **Project / proponent / site** | **Hazard and climate exposure** | **People/assets affected / inclusion** | **Siting/design/ecosystem implications**    | **Risk treatment / residual risk** | **Technical reviewers**               | **Planning/budget decision**           |\n|--------------------------------|---------------------------------|----------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|----------------------------------------|\n| \\[Project\\]                    | \\[Map/source/date/scenario\\]    | \\[Groups and service impacts\\]         | \\[Alternatives, codes, ecosystem/heritage\\] | \\[Measures, cost, residual risk\\]  | \\[CPDO/Engineering/OBO/CENRO/CDRRMO\\] | \\[LDC/LFC/Budget/approving authority\\] |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-J.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('bc8819bc-c6ab-5a33-9e7f-99dbf9dd581c'::uuid,'26c123c7-cb03-5d9a-8dce-52900f5e108d'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-K \\| Form 3-10 – Consultation and Inclusion Validation record\n\n| **Consulted group / organization** | **Date / accessible method**       | **Risk or access issue raised** | **Evidence / location** | **Plan or design response**          | **Responsible office / closure** |\n|------------------------------------|------------------------------------|---------------------------------|-------------------------|--------------------------------------|----------------------------------|\n| \\[Group\\]                          | \\[Date, language, access support\\] | \\[Issue\\]                       | \\[Evidence\\]            | \\[Response / reason if not adopted\\] | \\[Owner / due date\\]             |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-K.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('4863a38e-1755-5ced-a4e8-3832f8b05646'::uuid,'d323303a-0f9e-5c64-93d6-de5b941aebca'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-L \\| Form 3-11 – Corrective Action and Document Revision Register\n\n| **Finding / source**               | **Root cause** | **Corrective action** | **Accountable owner** | **Due date / resources** | **Verification evidence** | **Closure / escalation**     |\n|------------------------------------|----------------|-----------------------|-----------------------|--------------------------|---------------------------|------------------------------|\n| \\[IAT / exercise / event / audit\\] | \\[Cause\\]      | \\[Action\\]            | \\[Office / official\\] | \\[Date / budget\\]        | \\[Record / test\\]         | \\[Closed by / escalated to\\] |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-L.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
