lation, CLUP mainstreaming, M&E and communication                    | Official DHSUD training material; apply current technical parameters and prescribed tools                                                                                                                     |\n| PHIVOLCS GIS hazard-map download instructions and Hazard Assessment Services      | Source acquisition, product scale/availability caveats and limits of hazard assessment reports                            | Official PHIVOLCS pages; not a substitute for current technical manuals                                                                                                                                       |\n| DILG MC No. 2025-035 / Listo si KAP information                                   | Barangay preparedness and planning responsibilities                                                                       | DILG regional publication confirms initiative; use signed circular and current national quality tools                                                                                                         |\n| DILG Quality Assessment System / BDRRM plan template                              | Barangay plan review structure and quality assurance                                                                      | Use current official versions; legacy templates are not presumed current                                                                                                                                      |\n| OCD/NDRRMC PSCP Guidebook                                                         | Essential functions, BIA and continuity planning                                                                          | Listed in IAT References as project reference; exact edition and original file must be verified before final technical sign-off                                                                               |\n| NDRRMC–OCD Contingency Planning Guidebook (February 2020)                         | Hazard scenario and response planning method                                                                              | Supplied 8 November 2026 and applied to SOP 3-6 (CP Forms 1–11; activation and deactivation flow; the Incident Commander recommends termination). Confirm with OCD Region VIII that it is the current edition |\n| UNDRR Disaster Resilience Scorecard for Cities – Detailed Level Assessment (2017) | Good-practice benchmarks for scenarios, critical asset failure chains, risk-sensitive planning and ecosystem services     | Benchmark only; IAT crosswalk identifies its adapted indicators                                                                                                                                               |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-M.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('ae57fb41-b283-50b0-80cc-2f447151ebd7'::uuid,'3189595e-e334-59f9-829b-ac4fb4757c40'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-N \\| Glossary of Terms Used in This Chapter\n\nTerms follow RA 10121, the DHSUD CDRA guidance and the definitions used in Chapters 1 and 2. Where an official definition exists, it governs.\n\n**Table 3.12**\n\n*Glossary of Terms*\n\n| **Term**                                    | **Meaning in this Manual**                                                                                                                                  |\n|---------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Adaptive capacity                           | The ability of people, institutions and systems to adjust to, prepare for and recover from hazard and climate impacts.                                      |\n| BIA (business impact analysis)              | Assessment of how the disruption of an essential function affects people and the City over time; the basis for recovery priorities (Form 3-07).             |\n| CDRA (Climate and Disaster Risk Assessment) | The DHSUD-prescribed assessment that links hazard and climate information to exposure, vulnerability and risk, and to land-use decisions.                   |\n| Contingency plan                            | An approved, hazard-specific plan setting scenario, triggers, roles, resources and reporting before an event (SOP 3-6).                                     |\n| Critical point facility / lifeline          | A facility (hospital, school, EOC) or network (road, power, water, telecommunications) whose failure affects many people or services.                       |\n| Exposure                                    | People, buildings, production areas, facilities and lifelines located where a hazard may occur.                                                             |\n| Failure chain                               | A traced sequence from a hazard through an asset failure to a service disruption and its consequences (SOP 3-4).                                            |\n| Form                                        | The record a step is closed on. In MODE every workflow and protocol step has a form; the Manual''s form where one exists, otherwise the one-tap step record. |\n| MDA (Major Decision Area)                   | A place or issue where CDRA results require a land-use, investment, social-protection or ecosystem decision (Form 3-04).                                    |\n| Modelled potential damage                   | The value of exposed assets that could be damaged under a model''s assumptions; not an observed loss or an annual expected loss.                             |\n| Process owner                               | The office accountable for an SOP producing its result; others are responsible, consulted or informed (Section 18).                                         |\n| Protocol                                    | A step-by-step operational checklist run at the point of action (for example warning dissemination); it records who closed each step and when.              |\n| PSCP (Public Service Continuity Plan)       | The City plan that keeps essential functions running during disruption (SOP 3-7).                                                                           |\n| Risk Information Register                   | The controlled list of risk datasets with source, custodian, date, scale, access class and version (SOP 3-2).                                               |\n| SOP (standard operating procedure)          | The approved, controlled text in the Manual that states what is done, by whom, under what authority and with what records.                                  |\n| Validation status                           | How far information has been checked: reported, preliminary, field-verified or official (Geo-COP layers; IAT evidence).                                     |\n| Workflow                                    | An SOP made executable in MODE: a sequence of steps across offices over days or weeks, each closed on its form.                                             |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-N.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('dfa15af6-b982-5600-a9ca-8b2250c23faf'::uuid,'3a03dcd8-4583-513d-8a37-b0df0d1da45a'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# ANNEX 4-A \\| IAT AND MASTER REQUIREMENTS TRACEABILITY REGISTER\n\nThis register copies the IAT v1.7 rows for A6, A7, A8 and B1.2–B1.5 (8 November 2026) and the functional master requirements linked to each indicator in the Data Dictionary v1.1. Cross-cutting requirements MR-01 and MR-12 to MR-15 apply to every indicator and are not repeated.\n\n**Table 4.40**\n\n*Assessment Rows and Chapter 4 Procedures*\n\n| **ID** | **Indicator (IAT v1.7)**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | **Type** | **Score** | **Priority** | **Compliance** | **Evidence status** | **Functional MR**          | **SOP**                  |\n|--------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|-----------|--------------|----------------|---------------------|----------------------------|--------------------------|\n| A6.1   | Hazard-specific EWS operational for flood (incl. Anilao/Malbasag river systems), rain-induced landslide, tsunami (Ormoc Bay) and tropical cyclone                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | M        | 3         | Medium       | Compliant      | Pending validation  | MR-06                      | 4-01                     |\n| A6.2   | Warning thresholds linked to specific actions (alert levels -\\> pre-emptive evacuation, class/work suspension, State of Imminent Disaster request) in written protocols, built to take up NDRRMC impact-based triggers once issued                                                                                                                                                               | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-06, MR-16               | 4-02, 4-06               |\n| A6.3   | Last-mile dissemination channels tested to barangay/purok level (sirens, radio, SMS/ECBS, social media, barangay criers)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-06                      | 4-02                     |\n| A6.4   | Warnings issued in local language (Cebuano/ Ormocanon) and accessible formats (sign language, visual alerts for PWD)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             | GP       | 2         | Medium       | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-06                      | 4-02                     |\n| A6.5   | Designated public information officer and risk communication plan (incl. rumor/misinformation management)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | GP       | 2         | Low          | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-06                      | 4-02                     |\n| A6.6   | IEC program on hazards and preparedness with annual reach targets                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | GP       | 2         | Low          | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-06                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A6.7   | Templates and channels for public notice of a State of Imminent Disaster and of the anticipatory actions required, incl. sector-specific impact-based advisories and reach to geographically isolated barangays                                                                                                                                                                                  | M        | 0         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-06, MR-16               | 4-02                     |\n| A7.1   | Annual training program for city personnel, BDRRMCs, schools and communities implemented                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | M        | 2         | Medium       | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-04                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A7.2   | Participation in quarterly Nationwide Simultaneous Earthquake Drill (NSED) and hazard-specific drills with evaluation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | M        | 2         | Medium       | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-04                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A7.3   | BDRRMC functionality across 85 barangays assessed (e.g., Listo si KAP) with support plan for low-functioning barangays                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | GP       | 2         | Medium       | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-04                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A7.4   | Permanent evacuation center(s) planned/established and existing ECs meet minimum standards (WASH, privacy, PWD access, child-friendly space)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-04                      | 4-06                     |\n| A7.5   | Prepositioned relief stocks/food packs and non-food items with inventory and replenishment triggers                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | M        | 3         | Low          | Compliant      | Pending validation  | MR-04, MR-08               | 4-07                     |\n| A7.6   | Inclusive DRRM: GAD, PWD, senior citizen, children, IP considerations embedded in plans and services, with vulnerable-sector representatives confirming they were engaged                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | M        | 3         | Low          | Compliant      | Pending validation  | MR-04, MR-09, MR-16, MR-18 | 4-06                     |\n| A7.7   | Schools, hospitals and critical facilities included in preparedness planning and drills                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | GP       | 3         | Low          | Meets GP       | Pending validation  | MR-04                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A7.8   | Refresher cycle (at least annual) set for trained responders, EOC staff and BDRRMC members, with attendance tracked                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | GP       | 1         | Low          | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-04, MR-18               | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A7.9   | BDRRMCs can account for residents of affected puroks within 12 hours of impact (welfare check), shown in a drill or a real event                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | GP       | 1         | Medium       | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-04, MR-18               | 4-06                     |\n| A8.1   | Incident Command System institutionalized: EO on ICS, trained IMT roster, pre-designated Incident Commanders                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | 4-05                     |\n| A8.2   | Organized and trained response teams: SAR (WASAR/CSSR/HAZMAT as relevant), EMS/ambulance, fire coordination with BFP                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A8.3   | Response equipment and vehicles inventoried, serviceable and maintained (preventive maintenance schedule)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | M        | 3         | Low          | Compliant      | Pending validation  | MR-05, MR-08               | 4-07                     |\n| A8.4   | Emergency hotline integrated with E911 and dispatch protocol (call-taking to dispatch time tracked)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | GP       | 0         | Medium       | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A8.5   | Response clusters organized at city level mirroring national cluster approach (Food & NFI, Health, WASH, CCCM, Logistics, Search Rescue & Retrieval, Law & Order, Education, Protection, ETC, MDM)                                                                                                                                                                                               | M        | 3         | Low          | Compliant      | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A8.6   | Pre-Disaster Risk Assessment (PDRA) conducted before forecast hazards, with anticipatory actions recorded                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05, MR-16               | 4-03                     |\n| A8.7   | Management of the Dead and Missing (MDM) and Rapid Damage Assessment & Needs Analysis (RDANA) teams designated and trained                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | M        | 2         | Medium       | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A8.8   | Anticipatory action protocols by hazard and lead time: office-order templates for prepositioning (relief, medical supplies, animal feed, water and power for evacuation centers), deployment of heavy equipment, transport and personnel, pre-emptive evacuation incl. livestock and pets, CCCM, and safeguarding of critical infrastructure; aligned with CPs, Oplan L!sto and evacuation plans | M        | 1         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05, MR-08, MR-16        | 4-03                     |\n| A8.9   | Anticipatory social amelioration: families identified and prioritized using CBMS or the prevailing registry; data-sharing agreements compliant with RA 10173; local guidelines for anticipatory cash or vouchers issued with the CSWDO                                                                                                                                                           | M        | 1         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05, MR-16               | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| B1.2   | Alert/activation levels defined (e.g., White-normal, Blue-alert, Red-full activation) with hazard-based triggers and a defined EOC posture when a State of Imminent Disaster is declared                                                                                                                                                                                                         | M        | 3         | Medium       | Compliant      | Pending validation  | MR-05, MR-16               | 4-03, 4-04               |\n| B1.3   | Activation, escalation, de-escalation and deactivation procedures with designated authority                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | 4-04, 4-09               |\n| B1.4   | Concept of operations documents EOC functions: coordination, information management, resource management, policy support                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | M        | 2         | Medium       | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | 4-04, 4-05               |\n| B1.5   | EOC linkage to Provincial (Leyte) and Regional (OCD VIII) EOCs defined                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | M        | 2         | Medium       | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | 4-05, 4-08               |\n\n*Note.* Scores are provisional until validated. Indicators without a Chapter 4 SOP are served by Chapter 3 (A7.1–A7.3, A7.5–A7.8: training, drills, BDRRMC functionality, stockpiles, inclusion, critical facilities) or Chapter 6 (A8.3, A8.4: equipment, hotline and dispatch).\n\n**Table 4.41**\n\n*Action Plan Rows (IAT v1.7), Copied Without Change*\n\n| **ID** | **Recommended action**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | **Responsible office**                    | **Target**                          | **Status**  |\n|--------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|-------------|\n| A6.1   | Restore and insure the flood/rain gauges; set a monthly functionality check; write an EWS SOP (planned PPA).                                                                                                                                                                     | CDRRMO Operations & Warning               | 2027                                | Ongoing     |\n| A6.2   | Write the warning-action matrix (PAGASA/PHIVOLCS levels -\\> pre-emptive evacuation, class/work suspension, EOC level, SID request), built to take NDRRMC impact-based triggers when issued.                                                                                      | CDRRMO Operations & Warning               | Jan 2027 (with MOP)                 | Ongoing     |\n| A6.3   | Revise the dissemination SOP with non-telecom fallbacks (VHF, sirens, criers) and test to purok level twice a year with logs.                                                                                                                                                    | CDRRMO Operations & Warning; BDRRMCs      | Jan 2027 (with MOP)                 | Ongoing     |\n| A6.4   | Maintain; add PWD-inclusive EWS (planned PPA).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | CDRRMO                                    | Q3 2027                             | Ongoing     |\n| A6.5   | Designate the PIO and write the risk communication plan, including rumour management.                                                                                                                                                                                            | CDRRMO; City Information Office           | Q1 2027                             | Not started |\n| A6.6   | Set annual reach targets per barangay and report them.                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | CDRRMO Admin & Training                   | Annual                              | Ongoing     |\n| A6.7   | Prepare SID public notice templates and sector-specific advisories with channels to isolated barangays.                                                                                                                                                                          | CDRRMO; City Information Office           | Jan 2027 (with MOP)                 | Ongoing     |\n| A7.1   | Maintain; merge with the TNA plan (A2.6).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | CDRRMO Admin & Training                   | Annual                              | Ongoing     |\n| A7.2   | Maintain.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | CDRRMO                                    | Quarterly                           | Ongoing     |\n| A7.3   | Maintain; target low-functioning barangays first.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | CDRRMO; DILG CLGOO                        | Annual                              | Ongoing     |\n| A7.4   | Audit ECs against RA 12076/DSWD standards; prioritise retrofits for the 46 critical flood barangays.                                                                                                                                                                             | CDRRMO; City Engineer; CSWDO              | 2027                                | Ongoing     |\n| A7.5   | Maintain; add AA prepositioning triggers.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | CSWDO; CDRRMO                             | Before typhoon season (May 2027)    | Ongoing     |\n| A7.6   | Hold a short FGD with PWD, senior, women and youth representatives to confirm engagement.                                                                                                                                                                                        | CDRRMO; GAD Focal Point                   | Q1 2027                             | Not started |\n| A7.7   | Maintain; include schools and hospitals in the next CP tabletop.                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | CDRRMO; DepEd; CHO                        | Q2 2027 (CP tabletop)               | Ongoing     |\n| A7.8   | Set an annual refresher cycle for responders, EOC staff and BDRRMC members and track attendance.                                                                                                                                                                                 | CDRRMO Admin & Training                   | 2027                                | Not started |\n| A7.9   | Add a 12-hour welfare-check step to BDRRMC protocols, using purok household lists (CBMS) and